        "id": "EX-GRAM-G-hsk1-existence-teach",
        "kind": "teach",
        "title": "Say where and what exists",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "text": "Entity + 在 says where something is. Place + 有 introduces an entity there; place + 是 identifies what occupies that place.",
            "examples": [
              {
                "text": "书在桌子上。",
                "pinyin": "shū zài zhuōzi shàng 。",
                "meaning": "The book is on the table.",
                "audio": "6f7b1f49705a349329670624330f209933cda6ea18f4bcb115605d3dae393e6f"
              },
              {
                "text": "桌子上有一本书。",
                "pinyin": "zhuōzi shàng yǒu yī běn shū 。",
                "meaning": "There is a book on the table.",
                "audio": "a44d8624c3db6d441b7920978bd9469b17086f4063ebde5e877d0800b9880898"
              },
              {
                "text": "前面是学校。",
                "pinyin": "qiánmiàn shì xuéxiào 。",
                "meaning": "The place ahead is a school.",
                "audio": "0f1b05700c2a55021e49c01e1ad9708ac6993c614730515e1c3407631a652d17"
              }
